# review: the branch an agent pushed, read as its merge request shows it. --review=agent/refund
# fetches it from the local origin and opens on the first hunk; the panel marks each file M, A or
# D with its +n −m. c / C walk the hunks across files: the imports three lines apart are two hunks
# though the fixture sets diff.interHunkContext (#220), the redrawn PNG is skipped (#77), the
# deleted script opens read-only. The lines the branch deleted at the end of repos.py scroll into
# view down to the last one (#179), painted as deletions (#144, #165). d from a changed line into
# the function the branch added, [ back to the hunk; m puts the tick on the open file and takes
# it off (#162). Last, c after a d into a file the branch did not touch goes back into the review,
# to the hunk left once #239 lands (0.7.0 opens the first file).
caption review · merl --review=agent/refund fetches the agent's branch and opens on its first hunk
merl --review=agent/refund
wait hunk 1/1  file 1/8
caption c: the next hunk, across files; the panel marks each file M, A or D with its +n −m
key c
wait app/repos.py  31:1  [code]  hunk 1/1  file 2/8
caption the lines the branch deleted at the end of repos.py scroll into view, down to the last (#179)
key PageDown
wait self.orders.clear()
caption two imports three lines apart are two hunks, though git's interHunkContext would merge them (#220)
key c
wait hunk 1/4  file 3/8
key c
wait hunk 2/4  file 3/8
key c c
wait hunk 4/4  file 3/8
caption d from a changed line into the function the branch added, [ back to the hunk
key /
type refund_amount(o
key Enter d
wait refund_amount: via import app/refunds.py
key [
wait app/service.py  44:18  [code]  hunk 4/4  file 3/8
caption m puts the tick on the open file and takes it off (#162)
key m
wait file 3/8  viewed
key m
wait file 3/8  not viewed
caption on through the chart; the redrawn PNG is skipped (#77), the deleted script opens read-only
key c
wait hunk 1/1  file 4/8
key c
wait read-only  hunk 0/0  file 6/8  skipped 1 file without hunks
caption C walks back
key C
wait hunk 1/1  file 4/8
key C
wait hunk 4/4  file 3/8
caption d into a file the branch did not touch, then c: back to the hunk left (#239)
key /
type REFUNDED
key Enter d
wait REFUNDED → OrderStatus.REFUNDED (via OrderStatus)
key c
wait :1  [code]  hunk
# Last, a deletion taller than the pane is read going down (#279): the agent deletes most of
# tests/test_service.py in your checkout, and on a pane of 20 rows Down from the line above it
# scrolls its lines in one row per press, the cursor waiting on its line, where 0.7.0 jumped past
# them; Ctrl+D goes on half a pane.
caption a deletion taller than the pane: Down scrolls it in row by row, Ctrl+D half a pane (#279)
run python3 -c "p = 'tests/test_service.py'; l = open(p).readlines(); open(p, 'w').writelines(l[:4] + l[45:])"
size 185x20
wait M test_service.py
key o
type test_service
key Enter Down*3
wait tests/test_service.py  4:1
key Down*10
wait class FakeUow:
key C-d
wait def make_service(*orders):
